dzn: Copy a 3D image to or from a 2D one a slice per layer when the formats differ

vkCmdCopyImage between a 3D image and a 2D or array image copies each slice
to or from its own layer. When the two formats are not copy-compatible in
Direct3D 12 (R16_SINT and R8G8_UNORM, say), Dozen copies through a staging
buffer: it copied one slice into the buffer, then copied the buffer's
footprint into the layer with the whole region's depth, so a copy into one
array layer covered every slice. Direct3D 12 refused it, and the layers kept
their old contents. In dEQP-GLES31 copy_image.non_compressed, such a case
failed, and so did the cases after it in the same process:
about 5,300 cases on an RTX 4080 Laptop GPU and 5,600 on a UHD 770 under
WSL2. With one slice per copy they pass (all 5,976 on the RTX 4080).

